[0.0,"o","\u001b[2J\u001b[Hdistinguish touching from a 1 ms gap: distinguishing them means touching\r\nmerges.\r\n\r\nSo I read \"backward compatible\" as \"don't change the parameter or its\r\ndefault, don't make callers pass anything new\" — satisfied. If you instead\r\nmeant \"gap_ms=0 must continue to merge nothing,\" say so; that needs a\r\ndifferent patch (if gap_ms and gap <= gap_ms), and the regression test\r\nwould have to move to gap_ms=1 to have two distinguishable cases.\r\n\r\nSeparately, the nested-interval issue from before (line 19 taking\r\nevent.end_ms unconditionally) is untouched here — it's a different bug and\r\nnot needed for this fix.\r\n\r\n✻ Architecting… (31s · ↓ 2.1k tokens)\r\n  ⎿ Tip: Use /config to change your default permission mode (including Plan\r\n     Mode)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────── fix-timeline-merging ─\r\n❯ \r\n⏵⏵ bypass permissions on (shift+tab to cycle) · esc to interrupt · ← fo…\u001b[1A\r\u001b[2C"]
